      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-diplomatic-disagreement-01",
        "title": "Diplomatic Disagreement: part 1",
        "setting": "project review",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Noor",
          "Liam"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "How would you put that more precisely?",
            "translation_fa": "چطور اون نکته رو دقیق‌تر بیان می‌کردی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Liam",
            "text": "I can concede that the proposal is simpler to implement; my objection is that simplicity is being treated as the main criterion.",
            "translation_fa": "می‌تونم بپذیرم که اجرای پیشنهاد ساده‌تره؛ ایراد من اینه که سادگی داره معیار اصلی فرض می‌شه."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "What distinction matters most here?",
            "translation_fa": "مهم‌ترین تمایز اینجا چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Liam",
            "text": "I would challenge the premise rather than the conclusion, because the conclusion follows if that premise is accepted.",
            "translation_fa": "من بیشتر پیش‌فرض رو به چالش می‌کشم تا نتیجه رو، چون اگر اون پیش‌فرض پذیرفته بشه نتیجه منطقیه."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_diplomatic_disagreement_scene_2",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-diplomatic-disagreement-02",
        "title": "Diplomatic Disagreement: part 2",
        "setting": "quiet cafe",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Leila",
          "Adam"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Leila",
            "text": "What is the practical implication of that point?",
            "translation_fa": "پیامد عملی اون نکته چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Adam",
            "text": "A constructive disagreement should make the alternative reasoning visible instead of simply saying the other view is wrong.",
            "translation_fa": "مخالفت سازنده باید منطق جایگزین رو روشن کنه، نه اینکه فقط بگه دیدگاه طرف مقابل غلطه."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Leila",
            "text": "Does the evidence justify going that far?",
            "translation_fa": "آیا شواهد واقعاً چنین نتیجه‌ای رو توجیه می‌کنه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Adam",
            "text": "My main misgiving is not the objective itself but the assumption that the same approach will work in every context.",
            "translation_fa": "نگرانی اصلی من خود هدف نیست، بلکه فرض اینه که یک رویکرد در همه زمینه‌ها جواب می‌ده."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_diplomatic_disagreement_scene_3",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-diplomatic-disagreement-03",
        "title": "Diplomatic Disagreement: part 3",
        "setting": "professional workshop",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Maya",
          "Daniel"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Maya",
            "text": "How would you respond without making the disagreement personal?",
            "translation_fa": "چطور جواب می‌دادی بدون اینکه مخالفت شخصی بشه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Daniel",
            "text": "There is more common ground here than it first appears: we agree on the problem, but not on the mechanism.",
            "translation_fa": "اینجا زمینه مشترک بیشتر از چیزیه که اول به نظر میاد: روی مشکل توافق داریم، ولی روی سازوکار نه."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Maya",
            "text": "What could you concede while still holding your position?",
            "translation_fa": "چی رو می‌تونی بپذیری و در عین حال موضعت رو حفظ کنی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Daniel",
            "text": "I would not dismiss that concern; I just think it should be weighed against the cost of delaying the decision.",
            "translation_fa": "اون نگرانی رو رد نمی‌کنم؛ فقط فکر می‌کنم باید در برابر هزینه به تعویق انداختن تصمیم سنجیده بشه."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
